    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   remove-bottom-padding">
                <div class="header-one-column">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div>
                            
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        <div class="row one-column ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="key-points">
	
		<div class="key-points-module">
			<div class="article-key-points">
				<p>Below are examples of some scams and alerts you should be aware of.</p>
<p>This is <b>not an exhaustive list</b>, as scam tactics change frequently. These examples <b>did not</b> originate from CommBank and <b>are not</b> authorised by us.</p>
<p>Visit <a href="/support/security.html" data-tracker-type="richtext" dtmtracker="&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;">CommBank Safe</a> to learn how to better protect yourself.</p>

			</div>
		</div>
	


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-two-columns">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>September 2026 - Investment scams</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        
                        <div class="row two-column  ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>There has been a rise in investment scams on social media, with cryptocurrency scams continuing to be common. </p>
<h3>How these scams often play out:</h3>
<ul><li>Investment opportunities on social media, messaging apps, online ads or unexpected phone calls.</li><li>Pressure to act quickly with promises of high or guaranteed returns with little to no risk.</li><li>Follow up personal service messages on messaging apps or through phone calls to build trust.</li><li>Often scammers allow small withdrawals early on to make the investment appear genuine before encouraging larger deposits. They may also use official-looking documentation to appear genuine.</li></ul>
<h3>Ways to help protect yourself:</h3>
<ul><li>Research before sending money. Search the name of the investment and the word ‘scam’ for independent reviews</li><li>Search the financial adviser or investment company on <a href="https://moneysmart.gov.au/check-and-report-scams/investor-alert-list" target="_blank" data-tracker-locationid="sept_investment-scams_investor-alert-list" data-tracker-type="richtext" dtmtracker="&#64;&#64;sept_investment-scams_investor-alert-list&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;" rel="noopener noreferrer">MoneySmart’s Investor Alert List</a></li></ul>
<p>If you&#39;re unsure whether an investment opportunity is genuine, take time to verify it before transferring money.</p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="video">
    
        <div class="video-module standard-spacing  video-with-desc">
            
            
            
                <div class="video-wrapper">
                    
                    <div class="video">
                        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/PjA6KMxhWX8?rel=0&wmode=transparent&showinfo=0" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                    </div>
                    
                        
                    
                </div>
            
            
        </div>
    


    

</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-one-column">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>September 2026 - AUSTRAC Impersonation Scam Alert</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        <div class="row one-column ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>AUSTRAC has warned of scammers impersonating the agency and its staff through emails, phone calls, fake websites, and messaging apps. Scammers are using AUSTRAC branding and the names of real officials to pressure people into making payments, sharing personal information, or transferring funds.</p>
<p><b>AUSTRAC will never unexpectedly request payments, ask for sensitive information via unofficial channels, or direct you to communicate through apps such as WhatsApp or Telegram.</b> If you are contacted by someone claiming to be from AUSTRAC, stop, verify through official channels, and report it to Scamwatch.</p>
<h3>Stop.Check.Reject:</h3>
<ul><li><b>Stop</b> – Does something feel off? If you&#39;re unsure, stop and take a moment before acting.</li><li><b>Check</b> – Contact the company using verified and official contact details, not the number that contacted you.</li><li><b>Reject</b> – If it’s a scam, hang up, delete the message, block the sender and don&#39;t click any links. Change your passwords if you think your information may have been compromised.</li></ul>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-one-column">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>September 2026 - Watch out for fake NetBank logon pages</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        <div class="row one-column ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>We’ve recently updated the look and feel of NetBank. Scammers may try to copy this new design to make fake logon pages look more convincing.</p>
<p>They often send links in emails or text messages that take you to these fake sites, encouraging you to enter your details.</p>
<h3>To better protect yourself:</h3>
<ul><li>Never use links in emails or text messages to log on to NetBank</li><li>Always log on by navigating to our official CommBank website or netbank.com.au</li><li>Check for anything unusual on the page, like a web address that doesn’t look right</li></ul>
<p>If you receive a message with a link to log on, don’t click it and delete the message.</p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-two-columns">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>September 2026 - Fake car giveaways on social media</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        
                        <div class="row two-column  ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>We&#39;re aware of social media advertisements where scammers are impersonating CommBank and promoting fake vehicle giveaways.</p>
<h3>How the scam works</h3>
<p>Scammers are using sponsored advertisements on social media that claim eligible CommBank customers can enter a competition to win a new vehicle.</p>
<p>If customers click the advertisement, they&#39;re taken to a fake NetBank page that asks for logon details, personal information or other sensitive information to enter the competition.</p>
<h3>How to help protect yourself</h3>
<ul><li>Be cautious of social media advertisements promoting competitions, prizes or giveaways</li><li>Avoid clicking links from social media ads or download apps from unknown sources</li><li>Access NetBank by using the CommBank app or typing commbank.com.au directly into your browser</li><li>Report suspicious ads to <a data-tracker-locationid="sept_scam_social-media-vehicle-comps" data-tracker-type="richtext" dtmtracker="&#64;&#64;sept_scam_social-media-vehicle-comps&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;" href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#a9c1c6c8d18f8a9f9d92cacbc887cac6c487c8dc">hoax&#64;cba.com.au</a></li></ul>
<p>Remember, scammers often use trusted brands and social media platforms to make fraudulent promotions appear genuine. If you&#39;re ever unsure, verify through official CommBank channels before taking action.</p>
<h3>What to do next</h3>
<p>If you think you have entered your details on a fake site, contact us immediately:</p>
<ul><li>Call CommBank on 13 2221</li><li>Message us in the CommBank app, or</li><li>Visit your nearest branch for support</li></ul>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="article-image image">
	
		
		
			<div data-asset="/content/dam/dynamic-media/support/2026/sept-scam-alert.jpg" data-asset-id="ce4e63c2-d6a6-4492-b5ac-f635aa281158" data-title="mygov phishing scam" id="article-image-be203f2852" class="cmp-image" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject">
					
		    			
		    			
			    			<img class="cmp-image__image" itemprop="contentUrl" alt="mygov phishing scam" src="https://assets.commbank.com.au/is/image/commbank/sept-scam-alert?$Responsive_Align_Center_Top$&wid=469"/>
		    			
					
				
				
	    	</div>
		
	
</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-two-columns">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>August 2026 – Scam text messages claim rewards points will expire</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        
                        <div class="row two-column  ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item  image-bottom align-images">
                <div class="image-section">
                    
                    
                        <img class=" " src="https://assets.commbank.com.au/is/image/commbank/awards_points_scam_example?$W780_H416$&fmt=png-alpha&fit=crop" alt=" " aria-hidden="true"/>
                        
                    
                </div>
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>Scammers are sending <a data-tracker-locationid="phishing" data-tracker-type="richtext" dtmtracker="&#64;&#64;phishing&#64;&#64;&#64;&#64;" href="/support/security/sms-phishing-scams.html">phishing text messages</a> that impersonate CommBank and claim that rewards points are about to expire.</p>
<p>These messages may show a specific rewards points balance and create urgency by claiming the points will expire soon.</p>
<p>The goal is to get you to click a link and visit a fake website, where scammers may try to collect your banking details, card information or personal information.</p>
<h3>To help protect yourself:</h3>
<ul><li>Don&#39;t click links in unexpected or suspicious text messages</li><li>Don&#39;t reply to suspicious messages</li><li>Be cautious of messages that create urgency or pressure you to act quickly</li><li>Only access CommBank through the CommBank app or by entering the CommBank website address directly into your browser</li><li>Delete the message if you&#39;re unsure whether it&#39;s genuine</li></ul>
<p>If you&#39;ve clicked a suspicious link or shared your banking details or personal information, contact CommBank immediately so we can help secure your account.</p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    ">
                <div class="image-section">
                    
                    
                        <img class=" " src="https://assets.commbank.com.au/is/image/commbank/phishing-awards-example?$W780_H416$&fmt=png-alpha&fit=crop" alt=" " aria-hidden="true"/>
                        
                    
                </div>
                
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    ">
                <div class="image-section">
                    
                    
                        <img class=" " src="https://assets.commbank.com.au/is/image/commbank/points_scam_august-1?$W728_H696$&fmt=png-alpha&fit=crop" alt=" " aria-hidden="true"/>
                        
                    
                </div>
                
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-two-columns">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2><b>August 2026 - Impersonation scams targeting CommBank customers</b></h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        
                        <div class="row two-column  ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>Scammers are impersonating CommBank to pressure customers into sharing personal information, moving money, or handing over their cards.</p>
<h3><b>How the scam works</b></h3>
<p>Scammers may contact you by text, email or phone, claiming there&#39;s a problem with your account or a transaction that needs urgent action.</p>
<p>They may:</p>
<ul><li>Ask you to call a phone number included in a text message or email</li><li>Direct you to a fake phone service designed to sound like CommBank</li><li>Ask you to share personal information, security codes or banking details</li><li>Tell you to move money to a &#34;safe account&#34;</li><li>Claim your card has been compromised and needs to be collected by the bank</li><li>Ask you to place your card, PIN or cash in your letterbox for collection</li></ul>
<p>Scammers may use urgency, fear and convincing stories to make their requests seem legitimate.</p>
<h3><b>How to better protect yourself</b></h3>
<ul><li>Never share personal information, PINs, passwords or security codes</li><li>Never move money to a &#34;safe account&#34;</li><li>Never place cash, cards or PINs in your letterbox for collection</li><li>Contact CommBank using the number on the back of your card, through the CommBank app or via our website</li><li>Use CallerCheck when receiving a call from CommBank</li><li>Report suspicious emails and texts to hoax&#64;cba.com.au</li></ul>
<h3><b>Stop. Check. Reject.</b></h3>
<p><b>Stop</b> – Does something feel off? If you&#39;re unsure, stop and take a moment before acting.</p>
<p><b>Check</b> – Contact us using trusted contact details, such as the number on the back of your card or in the CommBank app.</p>
<p><b>Reject</b> – Hang up, delete the message, block the sender and don&#39;t click any links. Change your passwords if you think your information may have been compromised.</p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    ">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <h3>Impersonation callback scams</h3>
<p>Watch CommBank scam intelligence experts Shannon Brown and Zoe Ma break down how a bank impersonation callback scam can work.</p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="video">
    
        <div class="video-module standard-spacing  video-with-desc">
            
            
            
                <div class="video-wrapper">
                    
                    <div class="video">
                        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/pPVKerFPbIE?rel=0&wmode=transparent&showinfo=0" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen></iframe>
                    </div>
                    
                        
                    
                </div>
            
            
        </div>
    


    

</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-one-column">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>August 2026 - Calls from fake authorities demanding money</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        <div class="row one-column ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>Scammers are impersonating overseas telecommunications providers and Chinese law enforcement or government agencies to pressure people into sending money.</p>
<h3><b>How the scam works</b></h3>
<p>Scammers may contact you by phone, claiming to be from a telecommunications provider or a Chinese law enforcement or government agency.</p>
<p>They may say that:</p>
<ul><li>Your personal information, including passport or Chinese ID details, has been compromised</li><li>You&#39;re linked to criminal activity, such as an overseas bank account that has received fraudulent funds</li><li>You must pay a fee for an &#34;investigation&#34; to clear your name</li><li>Your visa may be cancelled, or you may face fines or deportation if you don&#39;t pay</li><li>You must meet with them in person as part of the investigation or to verify your identity</li></ul>
<p>Scammers may use threats, intimidation and official-looking documents to make their claims seem legitimate.</p>
<h3><b>How to protect yourself</b></h3>
<ul><li>Never share personal information, including banking details, passport details or visa information</li><li>Never send money to someone you don&#39;t know or trust</li><li>Never agree to meet someone who unexpectedly contacts you claiming to be from a telecommunications provider, law enforcement agency or government authority</li><li>Be cautious of requests to pay using cryptocurrency, cardless cash, cash deposits, gift cards, store cards or international money transfers</li><li>Never forward suspicious links or messages to family or friends</li></ul>
<h3><b>Stop. Check. Reject.</b></h3>
<p><b>Stop</b> – Does something feel off? If you&#39;re unsure, stop and take a moment before acting.</p>
<p><b>Check</b> – Contact the organisation directly using official contact details, or speak with someone you trust.</p>
<p><b>Reject</b> – Hang up, delete the message, block the sender and don&#39;t click any links. Change your passwords if you think your information may have been compromised.</p>
<p><a href="/content/dam/commbank-assets/security/docs/threat-and-penalty-flyer.pdf">Download our threat and penalty scam factsheet (PDF)</a></p>
<p><a href="/content/dam/commbank-assets/security/docs/threat-and-penalty-flyer-simplified-chinese.pdf">下载我们的威胁及惩罚骗局资料单 -- 简体中文&#xff08;PDF)</a></p>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    


    
</div>


    
    
    <div class="column-control">
    
        <div class="column-container bottom-divider">
            <div class="column-items standard-spacing   ">
                <div class="header-two-columns">
                    <div class="header-section">
                        <div class="header-content">
                            <h2><h2>July 2026 - ATO &amp; myGov impersonation scams</h2>
</h2>
                            
                            
                            
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="container content-container">
                        
                        <div class="row two-column  ">
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="content-module">
    <div>

        
            <div class="item    align-images">
                
                <div class="item-inner">
                    <div>
                        <p>Scammers are sending fake ‘tax refund’ and ‘urgent payment’ messages by text and email. These may look like they’re from the ATO and can include links, QR codes, threats, or refund offers.</p>
<h3>3 signs of a scam</h3>
<ul><li>Messages asking you to log on through a link</li><li>Requests to share passwords, PINs or other sensitive information</li><li>Urgent payment demands or threats</li></ul>
<p>If something feels off, don’t click links or reply. Always check by logging on to myGov or the official ATO website. Never share passwords, PINs, one-time passcodes or sensitive information.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><b>Remember to Stop. Check. Reject. </b></p>
<ul><li><p><b>Stop</b>: Could this be a scam? If a call, email, text or social media post seem off, stop and take a breath so you can think clearly. Scammers often pressure you to act immediately.</p>
</li><li><p><b>Check</b>: Verify before you act, get a second opinion from a trusted provider to verify any claims.</p>
</li><li><p><b>Reject</b>: If you&#39;re unsure, hang up on the caller and block the number, or delete the email or message. If your account has been compromised, change your passwords.</p>
</li></ul>

                    </div>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                </div>
            </div>
            
        
    </div>


    
</div>


</div>
                            <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-6 col-lg">




    
    
    <div class="article-image image">
	
		
<div data-cmp-is="image" data-cmp-lazythreshold="0" data-cmp-src="/support/security/latest-scams-and-security-alerts/_jcr_content/content/group_module_copy/group/column_control_51433/col1/column_control_19665_1280334684/col2/article_image.coreimg{.width}.png/1784506350666/phishing-example-mygov.png" data-asset="/content/dam/dynamic-media/support/2026/phishing-example-mygov.png" data-asset-id="dd7169c5-2377-45b1-8c63-030007853b29" data-title="mygov phishing scam" id="article-image-072ff62428" class="cmp-image" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ImageObject">
    
        
            
            <img src="/support/security/latest-scams-and-security-alerts/_jcr_content/content/group_module_copy/group/column_control_51433/col1/column_control_19665_1280334684/col2/article_image.coreimg.png/1784506350666/phishing-example-mygov.png" class="cmp-image__image" itemprop="contentUrl" data-cmp-hook-image="image" alt="mygov phishing scam"/>
            
        
    
    
    
</div>

    


		
	
